Package: altarr
Title: Lazy Chunked Arrays as ALTREP Vectors
Version: 0.0.1
Authors@R: person("Michael", "Sumner", email = "mdsumner@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A prototype exploring how far base R array indexing can drive
    planned reads of remote, chunked, encoded arrays when the array is an
    ALTREP vector with a 'dim' attribute and no class. Chunks come from a
    user-supplied fetch function, so any store (object storage, 'Zarr',
    'GDAL') can sit behind it.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 3.6.0)
Imports: stats
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.0
